@0    = ~My fair lady, you have not been yourself ever since the events in Suldanessellar unfolded. You have not said anything about it or the death of your father. Do you wish to talk about it?~
@1    = ~(Nina looks at him for a while, debating what to say, then finally speaks.) Your concern is appreciated Anomen, really it is but... I-I prefer not to talk about it right now. Please leave it at that.~
@2    = ~Very well I shall do as you wish but promise when you are ready to talk, speak to me?~
@3    = ~Speak to you? Just you only?~
@4    = ~No, I meant when you are ready to talk I am there for you. I am a good listener after all.~
@5    = ~(Nina offers him a weak smile.) When I am ready to talk, you are the first on my list Anomen. You are a very sweet man.~
@6    = ~Thank you for the kind words my lady. Shall we join the rest of the group?~
@7    = ~Yes, let us go.~
@8    = ~I've been wondering, darthiir, when are you going to get over yourself? Or perhaps you faerie elves enjoy feeling sorry for yourselves whenever you suffer a loss in life?~
@9    = ~What did you just say to me gol rathrae??~
@10   = ~I see you picked up on some drow words. But you heard me, Ninafer, so answer the question or are you too involved with feeling sorry for yourself?~
@11   = ~Leave her alone, Viconia! This is low, even for you, acting like this towards Nina!~
@12   = ~Tend to your own affairs Aerie. If I wanted your opinion, I would spit in your direction.~
@13   = ~I don't owe you any kind of answer you drow bitch! (Nina gets right up in front of Viconia, face to face then whispers.) When we are done with helping <CHARNAME>, any time, any where it will be me and you!~
@14   = ~While I would look forward to that meeting darthiir, you are missing my point. Right now you are a weak link in this group. You are distracted and dwelling on something that can not be reversed. You act like you are the only one who ever suffered a loss. I lost my family and my entire house. Now you either get a hold of yourself, become strong again and move ahead or feel sorry for yourself. Your choice.~
@15   = ~(Nina stares at Viconia then walks away saying nothing more.)~
@16   = ~Aerie why the sad face?~
@17   = ~I am so sorry for what has happened to you, Nina. It's very sad about your father and your home being destroyed.~
@18   = ~Thank you for your concerns. But there is no reason for you to feel sad for me.~
@19   = ~Yes I do. Friends feel for their each other, whether it's something good or bad. You have helped me ever since you joined us and I am thankful for all that you taught me. I consider you my friend for it.~
@20   = ~Friend? I keep hearing that word as of late. Friends is something I never really had when I was younger. (A sad look appears on Nina's face after saying that.)~
@21   = ~Well silly you have one here and probably more in our group Nina. Friends are there for each other especially in their hour of need. If you need to talk I am all ears.~
@22   = ~Thank you for your concren and being my friend. In time I may open up but not right now. Thank you my ... sister.~
@23   = ~Ninafer you have been looking rather worn down lately. Mayhaps it has something to do with what happen in Suldanessellar? ~
@24   = ~If you are refering to the death of my father and the destruction of my home life then yes, it has put me in a depressive state!~
@25   = ~I was only asking you..~
@26   = ~If you are going to ask a question, then ask it! But be direct and to the point, don't fumble around with your wording.~
@27   = ~Hold right there. There is no need for talking to me like that. I was being a concerned friend by asking you what is wrong. I did not want to be direct for fear of bring up memories that would cause you distress.~
@28   = ~You are right and I'm sorry for snapping at you like that. These recent events is hard for me to absorb. It brings back what few memories I have of my parents, my biological parents. Now I lose another father, another person very close to me, another home... I'm sorry, I can't talk about this any more.~
@29   = ~If you wish. I am here if you want to talk more on this though.~
@30   = ~Nina have you seen Boo lately? I've not seen him for a long time. I hope he has not gotten lost.~
@31   = ~As a matter of fact I have seen him. He is right here in my pocket.~
@32   = ~What is Boo doing with you? I hope Boo has not been stealing food from Nina again!~
@33   = ~Settle down, Minsc. Boo has not been stealing food from me this time. As a matter of fact he snuggled up with me while you were away. Here take him.~
@34   = ~Minsc is glad that Boo is making nice with Nina. Yes! We are one big happy family now!~
@35   = ~I wouldn't go that far.~
@36   = ~Then Minsc will go farther then! You see, we have been traveling for so long and have become friends. A group of friends that has gone for many miles with each other, seen many battles, gone through good and bad times, becomes something like a family. True this is!~
@37   = ~Ummm.. yes that is true. I-I never looked at it like that. W-we are something like a family that is true. I... well nevermind. We n-need to get going.~
@38   = ~What's that on Nina's cheek? A tear? Tears of happiness?~
@39   = ~N-no it's just...... it's just some dust that blew in my eyes, nothing more.~
@40   = ~You can't fool Minsc or Boo for that matter! We know better.~
@41   = ~(Nina gives Minsc a smile. Even though she would not say it, but she would miss those two greatly when their days of adventuring would come to an end.)~
@42   = ~Hey Anomen, I-I was wondering if we could talk. I-I am ready to speak with you about the events that took place in Suldanessellar.~
@43   = ~If you are ready to talk I will listen.~
@44   = ~I took the lost of my foster father very hard. It's not the first time I lost a family. I lost my family when I was young to a band of drow raiders. I do not have memories of them, I only possess some of their belongings, like my mother's ring. A-and now I have lost another father, friends and family... (Nina's voice trails off.)~
@45   = ~Take your time Nina, don't rush it.~
@46   = ~T-thank you. I've lost two families, friends dead, my home in ruins and I've alienated <CHARNAME> by not telling <PRO_HIMHER> of my mission.~
@47   = ~I am sorry for what you have been through with the loses you have endured, my lady. You are strong and you will heal over time.~
@48   = ~Do not worry about <CHARNAME> either. <PRO_HESHE> understands that you were under orders to do your mission, I doubt <PRO_HESHE> holds any malice towards you for it.~
@49   = ~I hope <PRO_HESHE> understands. I really do respect <PRO_HIMHER> as a leader and a friend, at least on my part. Thank you for listening to me, you're a great friend.~
@50   = ~You are most welcomed my dear lady.~
@51   = ~(Nina kisses Anomen on the cheek, she stops and looks into his eyes. She embraces him and brings her lips to his and kisses him passionately.) I do love you so, my knight in shining armor.~
@52   = ~I love you as well my, Lady Ninafer. (They embrace each other again then walk away to find a place to be alone.)~
@53   = ~It seems odd having you in the party Sarevok.~
@54   = ~Why is that elf?~
@55   = ~You did try to kill <CHARNAME> in Baldur's Gate. It seems <PRO_HESHE> is quite forgiving in your acts. Another thing, you may address me as Ninafer, not 'elf'.~
@56   = ~Indeed <PRO_HESHE> is forgiving, perhaps foolish. I will remain loyal to <CHARNAME>, Nina, do not worry about that.~
@57   = ~In your case it's Ninafer.~
@58   = ~Anything you say elf.~
@59   = ~Nina, you seem different since we first met. You are no longer driven and uptight.~
@60   = ~Uptight? I did and still do, take things seriously. I just don't make it obvious now.~
@61   = ~Speaking of changes, I see you haven't changed much.~
@62   = ~Ohh? What do you mean?~
@63   = ~You still give away our hard earned gold to beggers and street urchins.~
@64   = ~Well they need it more than we do...~
@65   = ~Save it Nalia. I've aleardy heard your same song and dance tale, over and over again.~
@66   = ~This is a wonderful day.~
@67   = ~Glad to see that you're feeling better.~
@68   = ~That I am. It just took some time for me to get over the death of my father.~
@69   = ~That's good to hear. Time heals.~
@70   = ~It does indeed. Thank you for being concerned.~
@71   = ~I do so love being back in the woods once again! The smell of the flowers is just so invigorating. Speaking of flowers, Cernd did you turn those rose pedals I gave you into a tea yet?~
@72   = ~Yes I did. I have it in my pouch. Would you like some now?~
@73   = ~Yes I would, thank you. I believe it's close to tea time any way. Hmmmm. There appears to a slightly different taste to this than usual.~
@74   = ~Ahh you noticed the slight taste. I added some Zandar root. Zandar root is good for keeping fatigue at bay plus it will help wounds heal quicker.~
@75   = ~Well, that is fine but there is one problem with what you did.~
@76   = ~And what is that?~
@77   = ~The problem with Zandor root is it makes me break out in hives. Next time when you have a great idea about adding something to my tea, tell me about it. Okay?~
@78   = ~Opps sorry about that. I'll consult you next time before I add a surprise to your food or drink.~
@79   = ~Thank you I would appreciate that. Oh dear I'm breaking out now.~
@80   = ~So Imoen, how goes your studies?~
@81   = ~Not very good. Some of these spells are just too hard for me to memorize! I think I have it down, then cast the spell and it fails.~
@82   = ~Oh? How often do you spend time studying a spell?~
@83   = ~Let me see. The last spell that failed I studied for an hour. Jeezes an hour lost that I could have been spent on something fun like pick pocketing the local people.~
@84   = ~An hour?!?! Some of these spells take a day if not days to get down just right. And that is for someone who is skillful in magic. Imoen you need to do better with your studying I'm afraid.~
@85   = ~Oh that's just great! Now you sound like one of those stuffy tutors that me and <CHARNAME> had to put up with at Candlekeep.~
@86   = ~Stuffy? I am not stuffy. Magic is a beuatiful thing Imoen. One must dedicate their time too master it, too become one with it. A few fleeting hours is not going to do that.~
@87   = ~Ya know Nina, you would make a good teacher.~
@88   = ~Well thank you Imoen.~
@89   = ~Let me finish by saying this, you would make a good teacher for stuffy old wizards. Heh!~
@90   = ~Oh that's funny. Ha Ha. Right.~
